  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 107 AM MST Tue Nov 24 2026\n\nLittle change to the forecast. Ridge of high pressure will \nproduce dry weather into Wednesday. A weak shortwave trough will\npass through Wednesday into Thursday, this will bring cloudy \nconditions but no precipitation. The upper level flow turns \nnorthwesterly for late week and into the weekend. This will \nspread more moisture into the region, but the central mountains \nwill act to shadow a large portion of south and east Idaho. So, \nthe better chances for precipitation will be around Stanley to \nChallis and around the Island Park/Driggs region. Late weekend \ninto early next week, models show additional chances for \nprecipitation but not much agreement on how the overarching \nweather system responsible for that moisture will behave.",
